    "summary": "Bow harp with an arched wood neck with eight pegs. Roughly oval sound-box is made of skin stretched around a wooden frame. Single small circular sound-hole. Back of sound-box is decorated with gut ? strings coloured natural, red and brown sewn through skin, central section is undecorated. Eight gut ? strings, three coloured red, attached to wood rod which is fixed under surface of sound-box. Outer string is broken in middle and has been replaced with cotton thread knotted on to the gut. Seven reptile skin-covered bands encircle neck between pegs.",
